      "transcriptionStatus": "source-verified",
      "gradingStatus": "official key verified",
      "hasFigure": false,
      "solution": "On the increasing side of the weight–age curve, two different ages have different weights; the same holds on the decreasing side. To have equal weights at distinct ages, the brothers must lie on opposite sides of the maximum at age 50. Thus a₁<50<a₂, option B.",
